 "notes": [
  "Scores compare monthly regional totals of Aqua-equivalent counts against real MODIS Aqua, on test data the models never saw (2019 onward), and on NOAA-20, which was never used in fitting.",
  "'overall' pools all region-months; because regions differ a lot in size this inflates r2, so read the per-region numbers too.",
  "Winner B_qm chosen by lowest mean normalized RMSE across regions on the holdout (0.169 vs global ratio 0.259).",
  "From 2022 Terra and Aqua drift off their original overpass times (results/overpass_times.md), so the MODIS reference itself changes; holdout scores for 2019-2021 and 2022+ are reported separately in results/metrics_detail.json.",
  "Land-cover groups (MCD12Q1) used for: amazon, australia, texas.",
  "The harmonized record is on the Terra+Aqua scale: Aqua-equivalent counts are multiplied by the 2003-2018 (Terra+Aqua)/Aqua ratio per region, day/night and calendar month.",
  "Harmonized FRP (mefrp) uses one global FRP ratio and is not separately validated."
 ],
